rmat="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOAGOSEI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FURUYA NAGAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUYA, NAGAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A reaction layer material for gas diffusion electrodes which is obtained by mixing an aqueous solution containing a surfactant and fine hydrophilic particles and hydrophobic carbon black both dispersed therein with a polytetrafluoroethylene dispersion, adding a binder thereto, and homogenizing the mixture, wherein the average particle diameter rs of the hydrophilic particles, that rc of the carbon black, and that rp of the polytetrafluoroethylene particles contained in the dispersion satisfy the relationships D=rc/rp, 0.5&lt;D&lt;2, and rs&lt;2rp.  A jet mill is used for dispersing the carbon black. The fluid obtained by adding the binder is spray-dried or applied by spraying.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un matériau pour former la couche réactive d'électrodes de diffusion gazeuse. On prépare ce matériau en mélangeant une solution aqueuse contenant un tensioactif, dans laquelle sont dispersées et des particules fines hydrophiles et du noir de carbone hydrophobe, avec une dispersion de polytétrafluoroéthylène, en ajoutant un liant à ce mélange puis en l'homogénéisant. Le diamètre rs moyen des particules hydrophiles et celui rc du noir de carbone et celui rp des particules de polytétrafluoroéthylène contenues dans la dispersion obéissent aux relations suivantes : D=rc/rp, 0,5&lt;D&lt;2, et rs&lt;2rp. On utilise un broyeur à jet pour disperser le noir de carbone. Le liquide obtenu après l'adjonction du liant est séché par vaporisation ou appliqué par vaporisation.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>